'' The shapes MSVC's headers are written with. An anonymous member of a named record, or
'' of a typedef of one, is one only under MS extensions -- windows-x86_64 -- where clang gives
'' it an implicit field that the record's children never show; its members are the
'' record's own. An unnamed bit-field is padding and takes a synthetic name. A dllimport
'' variable is 'extern import', and a static inline function has no symbol to bind: not declared, and named in
'' the header's ledger (tiko-vendor RFC-0001 D5).
'' Every record is laid out by tiko and checked against clang, so a lost member is a
'' refusal here rather than a short record. See src/msext.h.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -cimport tests/cimport/src/msext.h -cimport-out -
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: __cimport_bits2 : 7 as long
'' EXPECT-NOT: declare function ms_inline
'' EXPECT-OUT: function  ms_inline                   static
'' EXPECT-NOT: tiko lays it out
'' EXPECT-NOT: in tiko's layout
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: type ms_by_typedef extern "c"
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: a as long
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: extra as culong
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: x as long
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: extern import ms_imported alias "ms_imported" as long
'' EXPECT-OUT[windows-x86_64]: declare function ms_imported_fn cdecl alias "ms_imported_fn" ( byval v as long ) as long
'' EXPECT-OUT[win64]: extern import ms_imported alias "ms_imported" as long
